  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In defense of the life and dignity of the victims in Guerrero&apos;s Mountain</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tlachinollan is an organization that has been working intensively for 30 years to defend the human rights of the most vulnerable and have managed to strengthen a relationship of trust with people who are victims of serious human rights violations and with indigenous communities. This closeness has allowed them to accompany groups and families of missing persons from both the Monta&#xf1;a region and other regions of the state of Guerrero. With this project, they will be providing support to victims of serious human rights violations in the state of Guerrero, especially to the parents of the 43 students who disappeared in Ayotzinapa in 2014, and to the families of women victims of femicide. The project is focused on accompanying victims of forced disappearance in Mexico and create networks within different organizations in Mexico that carry out work on this matter.</narrative>
  </description>
